<<~ ahu slot=`#/operator-rulings-2026-11-05`>>

!! Operator rulings 2026-11-05 (record each where it belongs)
"Browser + Node is part of founding" (B1 rises before the rite). "Land all before the rite, no 'build a now, b later'." "Multiple tabs will carry live sessions, and later can change face (ONE FACE per session later on the roadmap)." "realm" stays reserved for the DreamNet (a JavaScript execution context reads as a thread). The ceremony document approved. Terra and Luna readers approved when needed; an online reader 1-off approved. The 180 s CI-read pace (a pace for a tool's own reads at the web2 edge, never a deadline or verdict).

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/house-decisions-awaiting-the-operator-s-overrule`>>

!! House decisions awaiting the operator's overrule (record as defaults)
* The ward key in the admission, the ward proof of possession, warded approvals carrying the frontier (S3b D/E) — changes admission bytes; built as the default.
* "The asker seals" rewording: "the asker's session seals, on the vessel worker's thread, while that face's session stands unlocked" (default pending).
* A set-aside device's past outcomes stop standing for readers who see the set-aside (from the edge-frontier ruling "a raise shadows its target at once"); a refused cap tip reads the tightest cap.
* Sealing scope (from the 2026-10-12 ruling): every wiki content store and CAD seal; planes and boards stay clear by the waking-floor law; the catalog and daemon bag split per face (D) + floor-public (F), no vessel-wide content key.
* Timer saves sign under the session that wrote the change; the lock and stand-down flush first; an unbooked save waits in memory.
* Same-face tabs: one provider per face lit at the first unlock, each tab proves its own unlock.
* The ceremony hosts passphrase (ward + custody) and PRF (custody only) answers; PRF never the sole copy.
* The vessel reads its own durability (Safari's 7-day rule; Home Screen exemption).

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/the-order-to-the-rite`>>

